<p>The next key observation is that we don=E2=80=99t necessarily care about=
 the values themselves: we only care about the parity of each number (i.e.,=
 if they=E2=80=99re even or odd). Given this, we can simplify the triangle =
further by representing it as a binary triangle where 0 represents an even =
number and 1 represents an odd number:</p>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display:flex;justify-content:center"><=
img alt=3D"Image represents a 5x5 matrix, labeled 'position' at the top, sh=
